From 164db20814f77704f3d59a86148bdec132c58f71 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daehyun Kim <kimdhyungg@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 16:38:24 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] [CBRD-27237] Probe: savepoint, concurrent-update,
 relocated-row cases (local only)

Three throwaway probes next to RolledBackUpdateKeepsCommittedOosAfterVacuum,
to weigh fix options B and C with runtime evidence. Each expects the
correct behavior, so a failure is the defect showing.

- P1: ROLLBACK TO SAVEPOINT undoes the UPDATE, then the transaction
  commits. A commit-status gate (option B) would not skip this record.
- P2: T1's aborted UPDATE is vacuumed while T2's later in-place UPDATE
  is still active, then T2 rolls back. A reader snapshot holds T1's
  block until T2's UPDATE is in place. A current-record guard
  (option C) sees T2's version, not the original.
- P3: a relocated row's aborted UPDATE back into its home page deletes
  the old REC_NEWHOME with RVHF_DELETE_NEWHOME_NOTIFY_VACUUM.

build_heap_recdes_with_oos gains an aligned padding parameter so P3
can grow a row out of its home page.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
